DTSTAMP:20260712T000000Z
DTSTART:20260712T090000Z
DTEND:20260712T130000Z
SUMMARY:Diplo's Run Club Denver
DESCRIPTION:5K Run & Rave featuring a race through Denver's iconic neighborhoods starting and finishing at Cheesman Park\, followed by a post-race concert featuring Diplo + friends.
LOCATION:Cheesman Park\, Denver\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ouray-100-mile-endurance-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260712T000000Z
DTSTART:20260717T080000Z
DTEND:20260717T120000Z
SUMMARY:Ouray 100 Mile Endurance Run
DESCRIPTION:A brutal mountain race with approximately 42\,000 feet of elevation gain for the 100-mile distance. It is known for its steepness and technicality in the heart of the San Juan Mountains.
LOCATION:Fellin Park\, 9th St\, Ouray\, CO 81427
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:high-lonesome-100-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260712T000000Z
DTSTART:20260717T080000Z
DTEND:20260717T120000Z
SUMMARY:High Lonesome 100
DESCRIPTION:A 100-mile high-altitude trail race in the Sawatch Range of the Colorado Rocky Mountains with 23\,500 feet of vertical gain\, reaching an elevation of 13\,150 feet. The loop course features singletrack through two ghost towns\, over five alpine passes\, along the National Continental Divide and Colorado Trails\, with a 37-hour time limit. Established in 2017 and organized by Freestone Endurance.
LOCATION:Mount Princeton Hot Springs Resort\, 15870 Co Rd 162\, Nathrop\, CO 81236
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:10k-5k-10000-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260712T000000Z
DTSTART:20260718T080000Z
DTEND:20260718T120000Z
SUMMARY:10K & 5K @ 10,000'
DESCRIPTION:High-altitude trail running race at 10\,000 feet elevation. Features well-marked routes\, aid stations\, and Northside Kitchen donuts at finish.
LOCATION:Vail\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:audi-power-of-four-trail-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260712T000000Z
DTSTART:20260718T080000Z
DTEND:20260718T120000Z
SUMMARY:Audi Power of Four Trail Run
DESCRIPTION:The Audi Power of Four Race Series is a premier endurance race series utilizing the unique terrain of all four Aspen Snowmass mountains. The signature 50K Ultra covers all four mountains via singletrack and dirt road. The 25K runs the Government Trail linking Buttermilk and Snowmass. The 10K starts at Elk Camp Restaurant and traverses Snowmass down to Fanny Hill. Registration fee ranges from $100–$125\, opening January 1st.
LOCATION:Aspen\, Tiehack\, & Elk Camp\, Aspen\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:transrockies-run-pass-to-pub-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260712T000000Z
DTSTART:20260719T080000Z
DTEND:20260719T120000Z
SUMMARY:TransRockies Run - Pass to Pub
DESCRIPTION:A multi-day trail running adventure in Colorado. The race features two distance options (Half Pint and Full Pint) and emphasizes community building over a magical week. Participants can sign up to run or volunteer.
LOCATION:TBD
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:never-summer-100k-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260712T000000Z
DTSTART:20260723T053000Z
DTEND:20260723T093000Z
SUMMARY:Never Summer 100k
DESCRIPTION:A technical and wild ultra marathon through the Never Summer Mountains and State Forest State Park. Expect massive elevation gain\, remote trails\, and the possibility of seeing moose on this rugged northern Colorado course.
LOCATION:Gould Community Center\, 5450 Hwy 14\, Walden\, CO 80480
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:leadville-stage-race-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260712T000000Z
DTSTART:20260724T090000Z
DTEND:20260724T130000Z
SUMMARY:Leadville Stage Race
DESCRIPTION:A 3-day mountain bike stage race taking place July 24-26\, 2026\, in the Colorado Rockies at elevations from 10\,152 to 12\,424 feet. The Life Time Leadville MTB Stage Race presented by Kenetik features post-race dinners\, daily awards\, and offers qualification opportunities for the Life Time LT100 MTB. Participants compete for coveted belt buckles and age group awards.
LOCATION:Lake County Rodeo Grounds\, Leadville\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:never-summer-trail-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260712T000000Z
DTSTART:20260724T053000Z
DTEND:20260724T093000Z
SUMMARY:Never Summer Trail Run
DESCRIPTION:A challenging ultra-distance mountain running race taking place almost entirely within State Forest State Park between the Never Summer Mountains and Medicine Bow Mountains. Features extended high alpine ridge running\, two alpine peaks\, four alpine lakes\, and elevations between 8\,450-11\,852 feet. The 100km course includes 14\,500 feet of elevation gain with a 24-hour time allowance. The 60km course includes 8\,100 feet of elevation gain with a 15-hour time allowance. The race offers fully stocked aid stations\, finisher awards\, finish line meal\, and qualification for the Western States 100 Lottery (100km finishers under 23 hours).
LOCATION:Gould Community Center\, Gould\, Colorado
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:never-summer-100km-60km-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260712T000000Z
DTSTART:20260724T080000Z
DTEND:20260724T120000Z
SUMMARY:Never Summer 100km & 60km
DESCRIPTION:The Never Summer 100km & 60km races take place almost entirely within State Forest State Park\, running between the Never Summer Mountains on the northern border of Rocky Mountain National Park and the Medicine Bow Mountains near Cameron Pass. The 100km course covers 65.7 miles with 14\,500ft of gain (24hr cutoff)\, and the 60km covers 39.2 miles with 8\,800ft of gain (15hr cutoff). Average elevation is 10\,220ft with a max of 11\,852ft. Terrain includes cross-country\, jeep and logging roads\, alpine trail\, boulder fields\, and meadows. Wildlife includes moose\, elk\, deer\, black bears\, and bighorn sheep. Registration is capped at 625 total (325 for 100km\, 300 for 60km). A 'Dirty Double' option allows runners to complete both distances. 100km finishers under 23 hours qualify for the Western States 100 Lottery.
LOCATION:Gould Community Center\, Gould\, Colorado
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:never-summer-100k-60k-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260712T000000Z
DTSTART:20260724T053000Z
DTEND:20260724T093000Z
SUMMARY:Never Summer 100k & 60k
DESCRIPTION:A challenging ultra-distance mountain running experience taking place almost entirely within State Forest State Park boundaries between the Never Summer Mountains and Medicine Bow Mountains. Features extended high alpine ridge running\, two alpine peaks\, four alpine lakes\, and elevations between 8\,450' and 11\,852'. Courses include varied terrain from cross country roads to alpine trails with significant vertical gain (100km: 14\,500' gain/descent; 60km: 8\,100' gain/descent). Time allowances: 100km - 24 hours; 60km - 15 hours. Registration caps: 625 total participants. Western States 100 lottery qualification available for 100km finishers under 23 hours.
LOCATION:Gould Community Center\, Gould\, Colorado
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
