UID:san-juan-softie-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260712T000000Z
DTSTART:20260814T060000Z
DTEND:20260814T100000Z
SUMMARY:San Juan Softie
DESCRIPTION:100-mile ultramarathon starting and finishing north of Durango\, Colorado. Features approximately 19\,000 feet of elevation gain with an average elevation of 10\,000+ feet. Course traverses stunning San Juan mountain terrain including the Colorado Trail\, Engineer Mountain\, Wilson group of 14ers\, and Lizard Head. 38-hour cut-off with 11 aid stations. Requires satellite tracking device\, rain jacket\, 2 light sources\, gloves\, whistle\, hat\, and water capacity.
LOCATION:Durango\, CO (start/finish just north of Durango)
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:leadville-trail-10k-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260712T000000Z
DTSTART:20260815T060000Z
DTEND:20260815T100000Z
SUMMARY:Leadville Trail 10K
DESCRIPTION:The Life Time Leadville Trail 100 MTB is one of the most prestigious endurance cross-country mountain bike races in the world. Riders tackle a grueling 105.3-mile out-and-back course through the Colorado Rockies with 12\,304 feet of elevation gain\, reaching peak elevations of 12\,500 feet at Columbine Mine. The course features forest service roads\, high alpine two-track\, and singletrack terrain.
LOCATION:Corner of 6th St & Harrison\, Leadville\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
