BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lead-king-loop-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260712T000000Z
DTSTART:20260913T080000Z
DTEND:20260913T120000Z
SUMMARY:Lead King Loop
DESCRIPTION:A spectacular fall running event through peak fall colors in the Elk Mountains. Participants can run\, hike\, or walk the 25K Lead King Loop past Crystal Mill and through the historic Town of Crystal\, or take on the 8-Mile Quarry Climb along the Yule Marble Quarry Road. Includes post-race BBQ\, beer (21+)\, custom shirt\, and finisher medal. Kids 2.5K fun run around Beaver Lake. Benefits Marble Charter School.
LOCATION:TBD
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:run-rabbit-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260712T000000Z
DTSTART:20260918T090000Z
DTEND:20260918T130000Z
SUMMARY:Run Rabbit Run
DESCRIPTION:Run Rabbit Run offers 50 and 100 mile ultramarathon races featuring challenging mountain courses in the Colorado Rockies. The 100 Mile race (14th annual) runs September 18 with Tortoise (9:00 AM\, 36 hr cutoff) and Hare (1:00 PM\, 30 hr cutoff) divisions. The 50 Mile race (19th annual) runs September 19 starting at 6:00 AM with a 15 hour cutoff. A charity race since 2012 that has donated nearly $700\,000 to non-profit organizations. The 100M offers a $100\,000 prize purse with $20\,000 for first place—one of the largest in the world.
LOCATION:Steamboat Ski Resort\, 2305 Mt Werner Cir\, Steamboat Springs\, CO 80487
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pikes-peak-ascent-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260712T000000Z
DTSTART:20260919T080000Z
DTEND:20260919T120000Z
SUMMARY:Pikes Peak Ascent & Marathon
DESCRIPTION:The oldest continually held marathon in the United States (founded in 1956). Runners travel from Manitou Springs to the summit of Pikes Peak at 14\,115 feet and back down for a total of 26.2 grueling mountain miles with approximately 7\,800 vertical feet of elevation gain. A sister race\, the Pikes Peak Ascent (13.3 miles)\, is also held the same weekend.
LOCATION:441 Manitou Ave\, Suite 100\, Manitou Springs\, CO 80829
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:run-the-rockies-road-race-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260712T000000Z
DTSTART:20260919T080000Z
DTEND:20260919T120000Z
SUMMARY:Run the Rockies Road Race
DESCRIPTION:The 50th Annual Run the Rockies Road race features a downhill course along the Summit County Recreation Path through Ten Mile Canyon. The 11k course (100% downhill) starts at 8:30 AM\, and the Half Marathon course (75% downhill) starts at 8:00 AM. Both races showcase beautiful fall foliage and have a hard stop at 11:30 AM. Registration opens April 22\, 2026. Includes commemorative gifts\, finisher items\, aid stations\, professional timing\, post-race food\, and post-race beer (21+).
LOCATION:Starts near Copper Mountain\, ends at Frisco Historic Park\, 1 Main Street\, Frisco\, CO
